---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { EXAM } from "@/lib/constants";

const examGuide =
  "https://d1.awsstatic.com/training-and-certification/docs-cloud-practitioner/AWS-Certified-Cloud-Practitioner_Exam-Guide.pdf";
const certPage =
  "https://aws.amazon.com/certification/certified-cloud-practitioner/";
const repo = "https://github.com/Abdalla-Eldoumani/cloud-practitioner-prep";
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">
      About this project
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-soft">
      A free, open-source way to learn AWS fundamentals and prepare for the
      Certified Cloud Practitioner exam, built so a focused week of study is
      enough to walk in ready.
    </p>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">Not affiliated with AWS</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink-soft">
        This is an independent study aid. It is not affiliated with, authorized
        by, sponsored by, or endorsed by Amazon Web Services in any way, and it
        is not an AWS partner or official training provider. AWS, Amazon Web
        Services, and Certified Cloud Practitioner are trademarks of
        Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates, used here only to describe the exam
        this material prepares for. The lessons and questions are independent
        study material, not official AWS content.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">How the questions are made</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink-soft">
        Every practice question is original, written to test the concepts in the
        published exam guide. None of it is copied from the real exam, and none
        of it comes from leaked or shared exam content. Each answer explanation
        links to current AWS documentation so you can verify it and read deeper.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">How scoring works here</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink-soft">
        Results show a raw percentage and a per-domain breakdown, plus an honest
        readiness band: building, on track, or exam ready. The bands sit above
        the rough passing line on purpose, so a green result means real
        readiness rather than a bare pass.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink-soft">
        These are study signals, not the official score. The real exam reports a
        scaled score from 100 to 1000 with a passing mark of {
          EXAM.passingScaledScore
        }, calculated by AWS using a method that is not a simple percentage. This
        site never claims to reproduce that scaled score.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">The exam at a glance</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 flex flex-col gap-2 text-ink-soft">
        <li>
          Exam code {EXAM.code}, the current version of the Cloud Practitioner
          exam.
        </li>
        <li>
          {EXAM.questionCount} questions in total. {EXAM.scoredCount} are scored;
          the other 15 are unscored and are not identified during the exam.
        </li>
        <li>
          90 minutes, with multiple-choice and multiple-response question types.
        </li>
        <li>
          Scaled score from 100 to 1000, passing at {EXAM.passingScaledScore}.
          Scoring is compensatory, so a strong overall score can offset a weaker
          domain.
        </li>
        <li>
          The certification is valid for {EXAM.validityYears} years.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-soft">
        Sources:{" "}
        <a
          href={examGuide}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="text-brand underline underline-offset-2"
        >
          official exam guide
        </a>{" "}
        and the{" "}
        <a
          href={certPage}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="text-brand underline underline-offset-2"
        >
          certification page
        </a>. Always confirm current details with AWS before you book, since
        exam policies can change.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">Open source and self-hostable</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink-soft">
        This whole site is open source under the MIT license, and you can run
        your own copy. It builds to static files with no backend, no database,
        and no accounts, so you can clone the repository and deploy it for free
        to Vercel or any static host, or run it locally. Your study progress
        stays in your own browser and never leaves your device.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink-soft">
        Contributions are welcome: new lessons, more practice questions, and
        corrections. If you find a claim that no longer matches the AWS
        documentation, please open an issue.
      </p>
      <a
        href={repo}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="mt-3 inline-block rounded-md border border-hairline px-4 py-2 font-medium text-ink transition-colors hover:border-brand"
      >
        View the source on GitHub
      </a>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
